<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ngo Xuong Van</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 965</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ngo Xuong Van was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngo-quyen">Ngo Quyen</a>, founder of the Ngo dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duong-tam-kha">Duong Tam Kha</a> usurped the throne following Ngo Quyen's death in 944, Ngo Xuong Van overthrew him in 950 and ruled jointly with his elder brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngo-xuong-ngap">Ngo Xuong Ngap</a>. His death in battle in 965 led to the anarchy of the Twelve Warlords.</p></div>
